   "xml_index": 59,
   "xml_name": "PS1_059_TUE_Count Odd Digits",
   "display_name": "TUE_Count Odd Digits",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Write a Python program that reads a positive integer and counts and prints how many of its digits are <b>odd</b> (1, 3, 5, 7, or 9).</p>\n<p><b>Hint:</b> use the same digit-peeling technique from earlier questions (<code>% 10</code> to get the last digit, <code>// 10</code> to remove it), and check each digit as you peel it off, counting the odd ones.</p>\n<p><b>Example:</b> Input: <pre>123456</pre> Output: <pre>3</pre></p>\n<p>(the digits are 1,2,3,4,5,6 - of these, 1, 3, and 5 are odd, so the count is 3)</p>\n<p><b>Edge case (no odd digits):</b> Input: <pre>2468</pre> Output: <pre>0</pre></p>",
   "answerpreload": "",
   "mark": 2.0,
