  {
   "xml_index": 60,
   "xml_name": "PS1_060_TUE_Second Smallest In A List",
   "display_name": "TUE_Second Smallest In A List",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>You are given the <b>outline</b> of a Python function that takes a list as input and returns the <b>second smallest</b> element in the list. Fill in the missing logic of the function.</p>\n<p>The outline already sets up two variables, <code>smallest</code> and <code>second</code>, by comparing the first two elements of the list. Your job is to complete the loop that goes through the <b>rest</b> of the list (from index 2 onwards) and correctly updates <code>smallest</code> and <code>second</code> as it goes.</p>\n<p><b>The rule to update them:</b> for each remaining value, if it is smaller than the current <code>smallest</code>, then the old <code>smallest</code> becomes the new <code>second</code>, and this value becomes the new <code>smallest</code>. Otherwise, if it is merely smaller than the current <code>second</code> (but not smaller than <code>smallest</code>), it becomes the new <code>second</code>.</p>\n<p>You may assume the list passed in always has at least two elements.</p>\n<p><b>Example:</b> <code>second_smallest([17, 3, 28, 3, 41, 6, 12])</code> should return <code>3</code> (3 is both the smallest and, from its second occurrence, correctly the second smallest too).</p>\n<p><b>Example 2 (edge case - only two elements):</b> <code>second_smallest([20, 10])</code> should return <code>20</code>.</p>",
   "answerpreload": "def second_smallest(lst):\n    # lst is guaranteed to have at least two elements\n    if lst[0] < lst[1]:\n        smallest = lst[0]\n        second = lst[1]\n    else:\n        smallest = lst[1]\n        second = lst[0]\n\n    # TODO: loop through the rest of the list (from index 2 onwards)\n    # and update 'smallest' and 'second' correctly.\n    # write your code here\n\n\n    return second\n\n\n# ---- Use this space to test your function; comment it out before Check ----\n# print(second_smallest([17, 3, 28, 3, 41, 6, 12]))",
   "mark": 2.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "print(second_smallest([17, 3, 28, 3, 41, 6, 12]))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "3",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": true,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(second_smallest([20, 10]))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "20",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "print(second_smallest([5, 1, 9, 3, 7]))",
     "stdin": "",
     "expected": "3",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "lst = list(map(int, input().split()))\nprint(second_smallest(lst))",
     "stdin": "3 1 4 1 5 9 2 6",
     "expected": "1",
     "extra": "",
     "show": false,
     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
